<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Natalia Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1839 CE – 1843 CE · capital Pietermaritzburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Voortrekker republic in Natal, created after the victory at Blood River and annexed by Britain within five years.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voortrekkers">Voortrekkers</a> crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drakensberg">Drakensberg</a> into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/natal-colony">Natal</a> in 1837. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dingane">Dingane's</a> men killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piet-retief">Piet Retief's</a> party in 1838, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andries-pretorius">Andries Pretorius</a> led the commando that defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-blood-river">Blood River</a> in December 1838. The trekkers founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pietermaritzburg">Pietermaritzburg</a> and organised a republic with a Volksraad in 1839.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volksraad">Volksraad</a> held supreme power in a weak, quarrelsome government. In 1840 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boers</a> helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpande">Mpande</a> overthrow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dingane">Dingane</a> and seized thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/zulu-kingdom">Zulu Kingdom</a>. Farms were laid out across the uplands, and the Volksraad's plan to move Africans southwards alarmed the Cape government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>British troops occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durban">Port Natal</a> in 1842; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boers</a> won at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-congella">Congella</a> and besieged them, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dick-king">Dick King's</a> ride to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/makhanda">Grahamstown</a> brought relief. Natalia submitted, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> annexed it in 1843 as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/natal-colony">Natal Colony</a>, and many trekkers moved back over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drakensberg">Drakensberg</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/natalia-republic.jpg" alt="Natalia Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Himasaram · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Natalia_Republic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1839 CE – 1843 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pietermaritzburg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Andries Pretorius</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Dutch Reformed Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Natalia, Natalia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1841&amp;focus=natalia-republic" aria-label="Natalia Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5471 3259 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Natalia Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5791 3515L5791 3515M5791 3515L4997 651"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5791 3515h0M4997 651h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5791 3515h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5791 3515h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Pietermaritzburg. <a href="/atlas?year=1841&amp;focus=natalia-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
